    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d762">

                <pb facs="0816" n="712" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg712"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/5088: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-04-22T13:00:00+01:00">April 22, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 22—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. From the Secretary. Your 52, April 21, 6 p.m. The preoccupation which you
                    express under number 2 is I believe covered by article 10 of draft resolution,
                    text of which follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Notes with satisfaction that the said Commission will in accordance with
                            its decisions watch in such manner as it deems best the carrying out of
                            articles 1, 2 and 3 of which the last named provides for the complete
                            withdrawal of Japanese forces as before the incident of January
                        28.”</p></quote></p>
                <p>Committee of Nineteen is awaiting definitive word from the Japanese Government
                    and plans to call a session only upon receipt of such answer.<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d762-f1"/> [Stimson.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d762-f1" n="82" xml:id="d762-f1-content">
                <p>The Department replied in telegram No. 55, April 22, 6 p.m.: “The Department is
                    instructing Minister Johnson, as
                    suggested in your 85 [<hi rendition="#italic">86?</hi>], April 21, 4 p.m.,
                    repeating to him the first paragraph of that telegram and text of article 10 as
                    communicated in your 87.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
